diff --git a/docs/options.rst b/docs/options.rst
index 5c23bad..c136373 100644
--- a/docs/options.rst
+++ b/docs/options.rst
@@ -408,6 +408,18 @@ valid choices.
 Choices should be unique after considering the effects of
 ``case_sensitive`` and any specified token normalization function.
 
+Pass ``aliases`` to accept alternative names for choices. For example,
+``click.Choice(["fast", "slow"], aliases={"quick": "fast"})`` accepts
+``quick`` and returns the original ``fast`` choice. Alias names and targets
+must be strings, and each target must exactly match an original choice.
+The alias mapping is copied when the type is created.
+
+Aliases follow the same token normalization and case sensitivity as choices.
+If an alias conflicts with another alias or a canonical choice after
+normalization, conversion raises :exc:`BadParameter` unless they map to
+the same choice. Help, error choice lists, and shell completion show only
+the original choices.
+
 .. versionchanged:: 7.1
     The resulting value from an option will always be one of the
     originally passed choices regardless of ``case_sensitive``.
